      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "none-plain-opening",
          "status": "canonical"
        }
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "rule": "No ornament at the entrance: the door is cut plainly into the stucco wall with no carved or cast surround, twisted column, or Churrigueresque relief (mission-revival.c02). A carved/cast entrance surround is the single tell that converts the building to Spanish Colonial Revival. This overrides the semicircular-arch-on-squat-columns entrance otherwise inherited, which describes this style's own porch arcade, not its door.",
